SUMMARY:Stranglethorn Fishing Extravaganza (Predicted time)
DESCRIPTION:Predicted time: the dates are confirmed\; the start time on Ame
 ricas and Oceania is not. The dates and hours are the game's own calendar 
 data\, which gives them in server time. The Americas server clock is read 
 as US Central time: players say so\, and it has been seen twice\, both in 
 standard time: the weekly fishing contest (Sunday 14:00 in that data) bega
 n about 20:00 UTC on November 8\, 2026\, which is 14:00 Central\, and on N
 ovember 7 a player in Pacific time saw the game's clock two hours ahead of
  theirs (UTC-6). Blizzard has not said. Whether these servers change their
  clocks for daylight saving time has not been seen yet\; times from March 
 14\, 2027 assume they do.\nRegion: Americas (Americas and Oceania).\nServe
 r time: Sunday 14:00\, read as US Central time (predicted).\nRepeats: Ever
 y Sunday\, 14:00 to 16:00 server time.\nKnown through Nov 7\, 2027. After 
 that: not known yet (only one year of the game's calendar data\, from buil
 d 1.60.1.70862\, is read so far).\nA scheduled time from WoW Tracker's Wor
 ld of Warcraft: Forever schedule data r2\, checked 2026-11-08. It is not r
 ead from the game\; a realm can open early or late around maintenance.\nDe
 tails and sources: https://radmagelabs.com/wow/#forever
LOCATION:World of Warcraft: The coasts of Stranglethorn Vale
URL:https://wago.tools/db2/Holidays?build=1.60.1.70862
